Package: scorecraft
Title: Scorecard Engine with Scale Alignment, Cut-Off Strategy and Production SQL
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jose Evandeilton", "Lopes", email = "evandeilton@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
  )
Description: Production-grade scorecard engine for binary targets (credit risk,
    fraud, propensity), built on 'OptimalBinningWoE'. Selects variables through
    optimal binning, eight admission rules, hold-out revalidation with frozen
    bins and a multi-strategy consensus ('glmnet', 'xgboost', 'lightgbm',
    'ranger') weighted by out-of-sample performance; fits the points scorecard
    with an explicit, auditable scale alignment (log-odds regression on the raw
    score composed with the PDO map); sweeps cut-offs with frozen cuts; performs
    honest reject inference through a sensitivity band; monitors PSI/CSI with
    both the fixed and the sample-size-adjusted threshold; and emits production
    SQL in several dialects, with R-SQL equivalence verified by test. The audit
    funnel never drops a candidate from the report.
